 <p class="lead">A foreigner, whether or not resident in Spain, can set up a Spanish limited company (SL) with one or more shareholders. The company is formed by a public deed signed before a notary and registered at the Commercial Registry, and the tax identification of the founders taking part must be in place: for a foreign individual this is the NIE or, without one, where they will carry out transactions with tax implications, a tax number assigned by the Spanish Tax Agency. The legal minimum share capital is €1, but while capital is below €3,000 at least 20% of profit must go to the legal reserve and, if on liquidation the assets are insufficient to meet the company’s obligations, the shareholders are jointly and severally liable for the difference between €3,000 and the subscribed capital.</p><p class="lead"><strong>Grupo Avanza Consultores helps prepare Spanish limited companies (SLs) with foreign shareholders or directors, whether resident or non-resident. Based in Paterna, Valencia, we review the structure, documents and initial tax obligations and coordinate the formation process, with written English support and a quote before work starts.</strong></p>
 <p>We work with you in writing, in English, Spanish, French, German and Russian. In-person appointments by arrangement.</p>
