     <p class="lead"><strong>If you are tax resident in Spain, your US Social Security is taxed in Spain: the treaty allows the United States to tax it, and Spain, as your country of residence, taxes it too and deducts the US tax actually paid on it. A pension from past private employment is taxed only in Spain, and the Directorate General of Taxes (DGT) applies the same rule to payouts from a US pension plan linked to that employment. A pension for service to the US federal, state or local government is taxed only in the United States, unless you are a Spanish national resident in Spain. Where the United States taxes you only because you are a citizen, Spain gives no credit and it falls to the United States to relieve the double tax. Grupo Avanza Consultores in Paterna (Valencia) classifies each US income, prepares your Spanish return and applies the credit for US tax. We advise online across Spain, in written English by email.</strong></p>
